From 6edbd761d13ac6bc5acdecab964225e50c14e827 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:22:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/26] workflows: apply tools/pullify.py (pull model, pinned
 actions, unused workflows removed)

Generated by `python3 tools/pullify.py` on top of upstream cc53bf0, with
no hand edits. On an upstream sync, rdgen-github-bootstrap skips this
patch (see the trailer) and re-runs the script instead of rebasing
generated YAML.

Result per generator (windows, windows-x86, linux, android, macos):
- Inputs are version, cfg, build_uuid and proto. There is no zip_url and
  no GENURL secret any more.
- Builds come back as actions/upload-artifact rdgen-<build_uuid>-* with
  a 1-day retention. The rdgen poller downloads and deletes them.
- The /cleanzip, /updategh (STATUS_URL) and api-server upload steps are
  gone.
- Images come from $RUNNER_TEMP/rdgen-assets, patch files from
  $RUNNER_TEMP/rdgen-patches, and printer-adapter from this repository at
  github.sha. Nothing is fetched from bryangerlach/rdgen master or from
  the rdgen server.
- All actions are pinned to commit SHAs. The top-level permissions are
  contents: read, actions: write.
- Deleted: sh-generator-windows.yml, build-web.yml, clear-cache.yml,
  vcpkg.yml, docker-build.yml. Left: the 5 generators plus the
  workflow_call-only bridge.yml, third-party-RustDeskTempTopMostWindow.yml
  and fetch-encrypted-secrets.yml.

actionlint 1.7.12 (static release binary, checksum verified) reports no
new findings. The remaining ones are upstream's: the TAG_NAME env
references an undefined inputs.upload-tag, bridge.yml and third-party
inputs are marked required but have defaults, and bridge.yml uses an
undefined matrix.job.arch. Shellcheck findings dropped from 68 to 54 (the
removed curl steps).

